protocol/  and  network/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bedrock protocol codecs and the RakNet/NetherNet transports.

  Originally:  CloudburstMC Protocol   https://github.com/CloudburstMC/Protocol
  Forked from: Kas-tle/Protocol        https://github.com/Kas-tle/Protocol
               Kas-tle/Network         https://github.com/Kas-tle/Network
  Licence:     Apache License 2.0 (see protocol/LICENSE and network/LICENSE)

These are vendored rather than depended on because this project's copies differ
substantially from upstream. As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License,
the modifications carried here are:

  * Added hand-written Bedrock codecs for protocol versions 944 (1.26.10),
    975 (1.26.20), 1001 (1.26.30), 2168 (1.26.40) and 2169 (1.26.45), each with
    the packet serializers those releases changed. Upstream did not cover these
    versions when they were written.

  * Added the codec for protocol 2192 (1.26.50), ported from upstream's own and
    re-parented onto the 2169 codec here, since this copy expresses the 1.26.44
    scoreboard difference as a flag on the shared helper rather than as a
    separate codec. Three of its writers were made tolerant of a field an older
    version cannot supply -- the dimension default biome, the entity diagnostic
    position and dimension, and the environment attribute noise alignment --
    which upstream writes unconditionally and which is null on anything a
    pre-1.26.50 codec decoded.

  * Corrected serializers where a version's wire format was wrong or absent,
    including StartGame, LevelChunk, SubChunk, PlayerAuthInput, CraftingData,
    CreativeContent, ItemStackRequest, PlayerList and the entity-data type maps.

  * Fixed a direct-memory leak in SubChunkData: the render height map retained a
    slice that was never released, leaking 256 bytes per sub-chunk carrying one.

  * BedrockPeer closes its channel when the remote end sends a RakNet
    disconnection notification. Upstream only records the reason, so a client
    connection the server had already closed stayed open until it timed out.

  * Replaced network/transport-nethernet with CloudburstMC Network's current
    NetherNet transport (https://github.com/CloudburstMC/Network, branch
    nethernet, with transport-common), which adds the HTTP signaling Bedrock
    1.26.60+ clients use for dedicated servers.

  * Channels without RakNet framing are treated as RakNet protocol 11 without
    the 0xFE frame id (UnframedBatchCodec), and Bedrock encryption stays off on
    them since the transport is already encrypted.

  * Removed upstream modules and sources this project does not use.

